ention."],"finding":"The named problem is that the harness is optional/unused ('A harness nobody is required to use changes nothing'), but the chosen mechanism makes nothing required: the tier/report protocol is documentation and the report path lives only in an advisory `plan-review-eval:` commit trailer with explicitly no CI enforcement. The solution therefore addresses 'tell contributors which tier applies' (a proxy) rather than 'make measuring required' (the stated goal).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f363fa32eabfe3d74","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem + Approach bullet 'The report file path is named in the commit message under a `plan-review-eval:` trailer (advisory; no CI enforcement, to stay portable)'","norm_id":"n73795ab0cae8de3a","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contributor edits a Pass-3 threshold, ships it with no `plan-review-eval:` trailer and no tier-0 report, and nothing catches it — the exact 'nobody is required to use it' failure the Context names.","Two changes disagree on which tier applied and there is no machine check to adjudicate."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either (a) add a note in the ADR that the trailer is a norm, not a gate, and record the portability trade-off as an accepted limitation with the review-time coaching (not CI) as the enforcement path; or (b) name a minimal opt-in CI check (trailer-present-and-file-exists for diffs touching the routed paths) as the enforcement seam, keeping it off by default for portability.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no",